why:    strings.Contains(x, "") is true, so `looper learn bump <file> ""` (or no text) re-dated the first entry in the file, whichever it was, and exited 0. Measured before the guard: the first dismissal was re-dated today. A bump exists to keep one entry from being evicted, so an empty match quietly protects the wrong one.
